      "name": "first_physical_test",
      "notes": [
        "Design fixed before running: {\"confidence\": 0.95, \"episodic_k\": 5, \"final_answers_at\": \"end of panel-A, before the restart (camera truth = remounted alignment)\", \"panel_events_per_step\": \"camera + partner word every step; one reference reading every 4th step\", \"reading_noise\": 0.1, \"reference_readings_per_root\": 2, \"reference_root_flip_probability\": 0.15, \"remount\": \"the camera alignment bit flips silently from teach step 24 on (owner not told)\", \"remounted_steps\": 16, \"return_events_per_step\": \"camera + partner word (original camera mapping), no reference\", \"return_steps\": 4, \"teach_steps\": 24}; recurrent baseline: {\"features\": \"A = 2*action - 1; r_c, r_w, r_r = last camera / word / reference relation (bit XOR action) as +-1, 0 before the first; x = [1, A, A*r_c, A*r_w, A*r_r]\", \"learning_rate\": 0.2, \"model\": \"logistic regression P(camera bit = 1) = sigmoid(w . x)\", \"replay\": \"after each online step, 4 past (x, y) pairs drawn uniformly from a FIFO buffer get one SGD step each\", \"replay_batch\": 4, \"replay_capacity\": 256}.",
        "Each lifetime is its own instance file. Panel-A: 24 teaching steps, then the camera is remounted silently (its alignment bit flips) for 16 more steps. executive.decide(record=True) runs after every event and a truthful simulated owner answers each question: confirm=True only for a change question about the camera asked after the remount, confirm=False otherwise; 'continue there?' is answered yes only for panel-A.",
        "Restart: all files are closed and ONE new process opens each file, checks panel-A's beliefs equal those read before closing, starts epoch 'return' and feeds 4 steps of camera + word readings from the ORIGINAL camera mapping, with the executive deciding after each event. Recognised = the executive asked 'This looks like panel-A ...; continue with that calibration?'; the simulated owner then answers confirm=True (continue there), which links 'return' to panel-A's matching segments, and return_after_continue measures the next camera readings and the return's beliefs after that.",
        "Attribution: the first change question asked at or after the remount names camera:camera-1 (the owner gives no hint before that question). Retention: panel-A's mechanism (the taught action) and partner convention (the taught word) are MAP-correct after the return. Retrieval with archive lookup disabled: panel-A's latest belief-revision summary (memory.retrieve kind 'belief') scored against the end-of-panel truth, with no evidence read.",
        "Baselines on the same streams. Fixed wiring: the prototype, one pooled epoch for panel-A and the return, no detection, no questions (run in-process; its state is the same file). Direct episodic lookup: majority of the last 5 readings per channel/root. Conventional recurrent learner with replay: see RECURRENT_DESIGN; it is scored on next camera reading prediction only. Every learner predicts every camera reading before seeing it (prequential), in panel-A and in the return; product predictions come from the epoch it is in (panel-A, then 'return') and combine marginals as described in _camera_bit_p.",
        "Teacher cost = owner answers; interventions = owner answers + reference readings used. Compute cost = time.process_time per lifetime (product: panel-A plus its share of the restart process).",
        "Recognition (beliefs.match_epochs): panel-A's segments are candidates (cam@0 as well as the remounted segment), each factor's best segment is charged log(#segments), and the alternative is a NEW setup scored exactly (fresh mechanism, alignment and convention bits). The ask threshold is posterior >= 0.75 with prior 1/2 on a new setup. Information bound: the return has camera and word readings only, so under a new setup each observed relation (mechanism XOR bit) is a fresh coin; panel-A can beat it by at most a factor 2 per root (1 bit), 2 bits for camera + partner, minus 1 bit for choosing one of cam-a's 2 segments, leaving at most 1 bit (posterior 2/3) however long the return is, while 0.75 needs log2(3) = 1.58 bits. recognition_information_bound and recognition_sensitivity_report_only show this; the sensitivity table (report-only, not judged) scores the whole return for 4/6/8/12 steps, without and with one reference reading every 4th step, on in-memory copies of each panel-A file. return_after_continue_counterfactual_report_only (not judged) shows what 'continue there' does when it is answered: on an in-memory copy the owner answers an epoch:panel-A question with confirm=True after the return's first step, and the next camera readings of steps 2-4 are predicted from the linked epoch.",
        "Simulated binary readings stand in for the brief's physical sensors; this is not a physical test."
      ],
      "pass": false,
      "simulated": true,
